    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cenchrĕae</span></b> ,
		ārum, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κεγχρέαι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one of the three harbors of Corinth</i>, <i>on the Saronic Gulf</i>, now <i>Kenkri</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 17, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 1,
				10, 9</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 4,
				5, § 10</span></i>. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cenchraeus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-rēus</span></b> , a, um, <i>of
				Cenchreœ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 60</span></i>
			: sinus, <i>the Saronic Gulf</i>, Porphyr. ad
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				C. 1, 7, 2</span></i>.</div>
